# Prefer local agents (budget vs CI)

**Default: local.** Omit Task `environment`, or set `"local"`. This studio’s Cursor budget is **effectively zero**. The local machine can run implement, Node lint scripts, Bugbot, and Architect. Cloud is **not** a smarter model and is **not** an outage fallback.

## Cloud cost (always warn)

`environment: "cloud"` bills extra: VM + install + a **full agent per stage**. Ticket rewinds (Bugbot ↔ Architect) multiply that. **Warn before any cloud launch**.

## When cloud can be worth it

Cloud is a **clean CI-like environment** (isolated clone, run `.github/workflows/lint.yml` steps). That can matter for **involved** changes (large bank refactors, SW precache drift across many HTML files) because catching failures before push saves CI churn.

If the ticket looks like that, **say the tradeoff once** and **stay local** until the human opts in.

## Required to actually use cloud

Never set `environment: "cloud"` unless the **current user message** explicitly accepts the extra cost (e.g. “accept cloud cost”).

“Do it in the cloud” **without** that phrase → stay local, one-sentence cost warning.

## Not reasons to go cloud

Machine feel, ticket length, “cloud is higher quality,” or watchdog/stuck recovery. Retry the **local** model chain.

Full pipeline: `.cursor/rules/ticket-lifecycle-loop.mdc`. Outages: `.cursor/rules/subagent-watchdog.mdc`.
